      "source_excerpt": "Study Design and Duration; Study Flow Diagram; Schedule of Procedures and Assessments; sections 6.4 and 6.6; section 7.4 Prohibited Medications: \"This is a double blind, two-arm, 28-day, placebo-controlled study with approximately 120 infested\" \"After screening on Day 1, all randomized subjects will be dispensed IP (Natroba™ or Placebo) to apply\" \"at home later the same day as a single treatment over the entire body from the neck down to the toes\" \"receive a well-being phone call on Day 14 to continue to emphasize instructions to prevent re-\" \"infestation, determine if any concomitant medications have been used, and check for adverse events.\" \"On Day 28 (Visit 3), all household members will return to the clinic for safety and efficacy\" \"The primary endpoint of complete cure will be assessed in the\" \"SCHEDULE OF PROCEDURES AND ASSESSMENTS\" \"Day 1\" \"Day 2 Day 2\" \"Day 14\" \"Day 28 Day 28\" \"Visit 1 2 follow- follow- 3\" \"Day ± 1 2 3+6 14 ± 2 14 +712\" \"6.4 Phone Call (Day 14 +/- 2 days) ...................................................................\" \"6.6 Final Visit (Visit 3/ET, Day 28 + 2 days) ...................................................\" \"between study day 12 and 16.\" \"Subjects should not use any scabicide within 4 weeks before Visit 1, or use any scabicide, or\" \"rescue Permethrin, prescription or OTC medicated lotions, other than the IP during the study,\" \"through Day 28.\" \"There will be no washout of prohibited medications, subjects will be excluded\" -- The protocol describes a 28-day study and one study treatment on Day 1, followed by clinic visits on Days 2 and 28 and a well-being phone call on Day 14 (scheduled Day 12 to 16). Week values are exact day-to-week conversions using the stated 28-day duration; Day 14 is represented as Week 2. The Day 28 assessment is the primary endpoint and the follow-up visit. Recent scabicide use within four weeks before Visit 1 is an exclusion, but the protocol says there is no washout of prohibited medications; this does not establish a routine screening washout, so screening_washout is null. Conditional adverse-event visits are not included as routine visits. The supplied Schedule of Procedures and Assessments provides the visit table. Period boundaries and screening duration are not stated in a way that supports the schema's week-based period entries.",
